<figure class="cache-path" aria-labelledby="cache-path-title">
  <figcaption id="cache-path-title">How the cache stays subordinate to the source</figcaption>
  <div class="cache-path__flow">
    <div><h3>Identify the query</h3><p>Query and parameters, plus source-update watermarks where supported.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Read within policy</h3><p>A matching entry can be reused within its tier-specific lifetime.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Return source data</h3><p>A miss or cache failure falls through to a live query. Successful results can refill the cache.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="cache-path__boundary">When a required freshness probe fails, bypass the cache. When the source fails, preserve the source error.</p>
</figure>

